remstart
    THE GOD OF THE SEA
    an ending of the hidden game, the fourth one, and the last of the secrets of the night. the routines
    are in fish_routines_neptune, and the tests are in fish_tests_squid. see THE CONSTELLATIONS in
    fish_headers_squid for how a constellation is made.

    THE TRIDENT. the god shows his favor once his trident has been drawn in the stars. it has five parts,
    and each is a constellation: the left prong and the right prong (easy), the middle prong and the
    crossbar (middling), and the shaft (hard). the number of a shape is the number of its part. a part
    counts once its constellation has been scored, at the end of a night, and it counts for the rest
    of the game. the sky of a night shows, for each of its three kinds, one of the parts of that kind
    that the game does not have yet, and nothing for a kind that has none left. TRIDENT_DONE keeps which
    parts the game has, and TRIDENT_PARTS how many.
    ONE A NIGHT. a night gives one part, and no more: once a constellation is made, the others fade
    from the snow for the rest of the night, and are not looked for. so the trident takes five nights at
    the least, and one of them has to be spent on the shaft, which leaves the least room of any.
    THE BAR. from the first part of the trident on, a third bar is under the two bars of the coral, gold, and it
    fills up a fifth at a time. see fish_routines_coralbars. info mode has a spot for it, which says how
    many "pieces of a godly shape" the game has, and that all of them bring something. it does not say
    that the shape is a trident: that is for the player to see. neptuneStep keeps it up.

    THE FAVOR OF THE GOD. the fifth part of the trident brings it. once the board has settled, the night is
    over at once, and the fish all wake up. the fish over the middle of the board make way, up and down,
    from the middle out, and the ones under it swim off to the sides. THE WAY IN opens there: a blot of the
    ink of the night, which is not ink but the sky, full of stars, with the edge and the glow of the squid's
    ink (PortalEffect.fx). his temple comes through it, a few pixels at a time, with starlight on it as it
    comes (TempleEffect.fx): the steps, then the columns, three on either side, from the middle out, and
    then the roof, with the trident in it. THEY WORSHIP IT: while it comes, the fish that are left lunge
    toward it all together, over and over, and ease back, with a soft voice of the choir every time. the
    way in closes, and the fish swim around the temple, in three rings, in front of the columns on the
    near side and behind them on the far side. the words come: "Neptune favors you". he is never seen.
    neptune_finale does all of that, and the game ends the way that it does for the other endings, with
    CORAL_ENDING_NEPTUNE.

    THE MAIN MENU REMEMBERS THE GOD. once a game has summoned him, a cloud in the sky of the main menu,
    over the boat, draws itself together into his trident, from then on. it comes together out of wisps
    that drift in, holds a while, thins back out into wisps, and is gone, and after a while it does it
    all again, for as long as the main menu is up. it starts over whenever the main menu comes up. it is
    made of the stuff of the other clouds, with their colors, and in the day there are faint rays of light
    down from behind it, and in the evening its edge catches the gold of the sun going down. it fades away
    as the camera goes under, the same as the reef. the page of mementos has a line to turn it off, once it
    is there. TridentCloudEffect.fx draws it, and neptuneSurfaceStep, which frame_surface calls, moves it.
    the FISH_MENU_NEPTUNE environment variable puts it there, for working on the game.

    THE BADGE. the ending is kept on the tables and on Steam, with a trident for its badge. the ending
    was given only enough room for the first three, so its fourth value has a place of its own, above
    the others, where an older game has a 0: HISCORE_ENDING_HIGH_STEP in the number of the initials,
    above the modifiers, and STEAM_FLAG_ENDING_HIGH in the flags on Steam. see endingPacked and
    endingUnpacked in fish_routines_neptune.

    the "Tide" window of the debug panel (FISH_DEBUG) can give the game the next part of the trident, or
    every part, which brings the god.
remend

#constant CORAL_ENDING_NEPTUNE 4
#constant CORAL_ENDING_LAST 4
#constant PREF_ENDING_NEPTUNE 20
#constant PREF_MENU_TRIDENT 21

global TRIDENT_PART_COUNT = 5
global dim TRIDENT_DONE(10) `1 for every part of the trident whose constellation has been scored in this game
global TRIDENT_PARTS = 0 `how many there are
global NEPTUNE_ENDING_DUE = 0 `1 when the fifth part has come, and the god comes once the board has settled

global NEPTUNE_ENDING_HOLD = 0 `1 to keep him from coming, for the tests

` the badge. HISCORE_ENDING_HIGH_STEP is HISCORE_MOD_STEP times 16, which is more than the modifiers come to.
global HISCORE_ENDING_HIGH_STEP = 1280000
global STEAM_FLAG_ENDING_HIGH = 256 `the flag after STEAM_FLAG_SEED_PICKED, which was always 0 before
global TEX_BADGE_TRIDENT

` the pictures. setup_neptune loads them.
global TEX_PILLAR
global TEX_PILLAR_B
global TEX_PILLAR_C
global TEX_TEMPLE
global TEX_STEPS

` THE BAR
global INFO_INDEX_TRIDENT = -1 `the spot that info mode has for it
global NEP_INFO_SAID = -1 `what the spot was last told, so that it is only touched when that changes

` THE SUMMONING. the sprites are made the first time that they are needed.
global NEP_PORTAL_SPRITE = 0
global NEP_PORTAL_FX = 0
global NEP_TEMPLE_FX = 0
global NEP_PORTAL_W = 330 `how big the way in is, at the most, in pixels
global NEP_PORTAL_H = 220
global NEP_TEMPLE_SPRITE = 0
global NEP_STEPS_SPRITE = 0
global NEP_PILLAR_COUNT = 6
global NEP_PILLAR_OUT = 100 `how far out from the middle the outermost columns are, in pixels
global NEP_PILLAR_STEP = 25 `and how far in from that each of the next ones is
global dim NEP_PILLAR_SPRITE(6)
global NEP_SHOWN = 0 `1 while the temple and the god are on the screen
global NEP_PART_AT = 600 `when the fish over the middle of the board start to make way, in milliseconds from the start
global NEP_PART_MS# = 700 `how long each takes to
global NEP_LEAVE_AT = 1500 `when the fish under the middle start to swim off to the sides
global NEP_LEAVE_MS# = 1300 `and how long they take to
global NEP_PULSE_EVERY = 640 `THEY WORSHIP IT: how long a lunge toward the temple and back takes, in milliseconds
global NEP_PULSE# = 5 `and how far they lunge, in pixels
global NEP_PORTAL_AT = 2400 `when the way in starts to open
global NEP_PORTAL_MS# = 900 `how long it takes to open, and to close
global NEP_STEPS_AT = 3000 `when the steps start to come through
global NEP_PILLARS_AT = 3400 `when the first column does
global NEP_PILLAR_GAP = 220 `how long each one after it waits
global NEP_COME_MS# = 900 `how long a piece of the temple takes to come all the way through
global NEP_ROOF_AT = 5400 `when the roof starts to come through
global NEP_PORTAL_SHUT = 6400 `when the way in starts to close
global NEP_ORBIT_AT = 6700 `when the fish start to swim around the temple
global NEP_ORBIT_IN_MS# = 1800 `how long they take to get into their rings
global NEP_ORBIT_RX# = 150 `how wide the smallest ring is, either side of the middle, and how tall, in pixels
global NEP_ORBIT_RY# = 52
global NEP_WORDS_AT = 7400 `when the words come
global NEP_MAX_MS = 30000 `when it moves on by itself
global NEP_PART# = 58 `how far either side of the middle the fish make room for him, in pixels
global dim NEP_FISH_Y#(400) `where every fish was, when it started, so that it can be moved from there

` THE MAIN MENU REMEMBERS THE GOD
global SURFACE_NEPTUNE = 0 `1 once the god has been summoned in some game
global OPTION_MENU_TRIDENT = 1 `1 while his trident is wanted in the clouds of the main menu
global SURFACE_TRIDENT_FX = 0
global SURFACE_TRIDENT_SPRITE = 0 `made the first time that it is needed
global SURFACE_TRIDENT_X = 512 `where the middle of it is, across the screen
global SURFACE_TRIDENT_UP = 70 `and how far over the horizon the middle of its sprite is
global SURFACE_TRIDENT_START_MS = 0 `when it started this time
global SURFACE_TRIDENT_SEEN_MS = 0 `the last frame that the main menu was drawn, to tell when it has come up again
global SURFACE_TRIDENT_WAIT = 1500 `how long the main menu has been up before it first starts to come together
global SURFACE_TRIDENT_FORM = 6000 `how long it takes to come together
global SURFACE_TRIDENT_HOLD = 14000 `how long it holds
global SURFACE_TRIDENT_THIN = 4500 `how long it takes to thin back out
global SURFACE_TRIDENT_GAP = 7000 `and how long the sky is without it, before it comes together again
